# VII16 — the finite asymptotic bridge (sufficiency direction)

Real germs on `(0, ε)` whose iterated derivatives `0 … n` have finite right limits at the
origin. Glue the negative side to the Taylor polynomial of those limits. The result is a
genuine `Cⁿ` function on `(-ε, ε)` agreeing with the germ on the positive side — exactly the
